	of specialized financial institutions that conduct credit, maturity,
	and liquidity transformation without direct, explicit access to public
	backstops. The lack of such access to sources of government liquidity
	and credit backstops makes shadow banks inherently fragile. Much
	of shadow banking activities is intertwined with the operations of
	core regulated institutions such as bank holding companies and insurance
	companies, thus creating a source of systemic risk for the financial
