	system, which taxes land value before development and residual site
	value after development at the same rate is distortionary, discouraging
	density. The second, raw site value, measures postdevelopment site
	value as �what the land would be worth were there no building on
	the site (though in fact there is).� Raw site value taxation is neutral
	(does not distort the timing and density of development), but the
	estimation of postdevelopment raw site value would be complex so
	that assessment would likely be less fair and more arbitrary, contentious,
