	unintended consequences. This is not the exclusive domain of the
	qualitative theory construction and analysis that has dominated such
	thinking in sociospatial theory: it is also involved in mathematical
	theory construction. It requires a relational approach to mathematical
	theory, however, that moves beyond unidirectional claims of cause
	and effect, avoids deterministic and teleological thinking, and recognizes
