	in U.S. metropolitan areas over time. We estimate skill-adjusted
	wages and attribute-adjusted rents using hedonic regressions for
	238 metropolitan areas in 1990 and 2000. Within the framework of
	the standard Roback model, we classify each metropolitan area based
