  number = {4},
  abstract = {A central requirement in the design of a legal system is the protection
	of law enforcers from coercion by litigants through either violence
	or bribes. The higher the risk of coercion, the greater the need
	for protection and control of law enforcers by the state. Such control,
	however, also makes law enforcers beholden to the state, and politicizes
	justice. This perspective explains why, starting in the twelfth and
