  pages = {865--890},
  number = {5},
  abstract = {Three exchange-rate regimes--a float, a one-sided peg, and a cooperative
	peg-are evaluated and compared in terms of efficiency and welfare
	levels. The framework of analysis embodies country-specific monies,
	with the money of each country being used to transact in its commodity
	markets and its currency-denominated bonds. Welfare levels depend
