	class to each (e.g. residential, business, industrial). Over the
	last few decades, however, much attention has been focused on the
	need to reform the system. Reform advocates have criticized conventional
	zoning on economic, social and environmental grounds and have proposed
	a number of alternatives, including performance zoning and form-based
