	a limit on the social obligation of ownership, the U.S. Supreme Court
	has employed rhetoric emphasizing the purely economic impact of regulation
	rather than its effect on a property owner�s dignity or autonomy,
	as in Germany. Beginning with the assumption that both legal systems
