	characteristics that proxy for the presence of knowledge spillovers,
	labor market pooling, input sharing, product shipping costs, and
	natural advantage. The analysis is conducted separately at the zipcode,
	county, and state levels. Results indicate that proxies for labor
	market pooling have the most robust effect, positively influencing
	agglomeration at all levels of geography. Proxies for knowledge spillovers,
	in contrast, positively affect agglomeration only at the zipcode
