	procedure is no smoking gun. It was not the major cause of these
	divergences, and it generates no long-run inflation measurement bias.
	Nonetheless, it increases OER inflation volatility and can drive
	OER inflation far from its measurement goal in the short run. This
	article develops a theory of utilities adjustment and outlines a
